---
import "../styles/tracklist.css";
---
<section class="section" id="tracklist" data-section="Features">
  <header class="section-head reveal">
    <p class="label">Side A · Highlights</p>
    <h2>Eight tracks.<br>No filler.</h2>
    <p class="muted">Everything cloudrs is about, pressed onto one side. Hover a row to hear it in your head, open it for the liner notes.</p>
  </header>

  <ol class="tracklist">
    <li class="reveal"><details class="track">
      <summary>
        <span class="t-index"><span class="num">01</span><span class="eq"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></span></span>
        <span class="t-art" style="--a:#FF3D00;--b:#FF9A1F;--r:20deg"></span>
        <span class="t-main"><span class="t-title">Native, for real</span><span class="t-artist">Rust · GPUI · Zed's UI engine</span></span>
        <span class="t-badges"><span class="badge">GPU</span></span>
        <span class="t-wave" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span class="t-dur mono">02:14</span>
      </summary>
      <div class="t-notes"><p>No browser inside. The window is drawn on the GPU with GPUI, the framework behind the Zed editor, and the target is under 100&nbsp;MB of RAM while a track plays. It opens instantly and answers every click at 120&nbsp;fps.</p></div>
    </details></li>

    <li class="reveal" style="--d:1"><details class="track">
      <summary>
        <span class="t-index"><span class="num">02</span><span class="eq"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></span></span>
        <span class="t-art" style="--a:#FF5500;--b:#3A1400;--r:160deg"></span>
        <span class="t-main"><span class="t-title">The waveform is the seek bar</span><span class="t-artist">hover · preview · jump</span></span>
        <span class="t-badges"><span class="badge">Seek</span></span>
        <span class="t-wave" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span class="t-dur mono">03:35</span>
      </summary>
      <div class="t-notes"><p>Hover the waveform and the bars up to your pointer light up with a preview of where you'll land. Click to jump. Timed comments will be pinned along the track, right where they were written. (Try the player at the bottom of this page.)</p></div>
    </details></li>

    <li class="reveal" style="--d:2"><details class="track">
      <summary>
        <span class="t-index"><span class="num">03</span><span class="eq"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></span></span>
        <span class="t-art" style="--a:#FFC145;--b:#E84D00;--r:250deg"></span>
        <span class="t-main"><span class="t-title">A real queue</span><span class="t-artist">drag · play next · undo shuffle</span></span>
        <span class="t-badges"><span class="badge">Autoplay</span></span>
        <span class="t-wave" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span class="t-dur mono">04:06</span>
      </summary>
      <div class="t-notes"><p>Drag to reorder, play next, shuffle that you can take back, and endless autoplay from related tracks when the queue runs dry. The row you drag lifts with an accent outline so you always know where it'll drop.</p></div>
    </details></li>

    <li class="reveal" style="--d:3"><details class="track">
      <summary>
        <span class="t-index"><span class="num">04</span><span class="eq"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></span></span>
        <span class="t-art" style="--a:#FF4D5E;--b:#FF9A1F;--r:90deg"></span>
        <span class="t-main"><span class="t-title">Jam, listen together</span><span class="t-artist">peer-to-peer · no server</span></span>
        <span class="t-badges"><span class="badge badge-new">New</span></span>
        <span class="t-wave" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span class="t-dur mono">05:20</span>
      </summary>
      <div class="t-notes"><p>Start a Jam, share a link, and friends hear the same second you do. Only the state travels, over iroh, directly between you. The audio never leaves SoundCloud, and there is no cloudrs server in the middle. <a href="#jam">More below ↓</a></p></div>
    </details></li>

    <li class="reveal" style="--d:4"><details class="track">
      <summary>
        <span class="t-index"><span class="num">05</span><span class="eq"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></span></span>
        <span class="t-art" style="--a:#B83C00;--b:#FFD9C2;--r:300deg"></span>
        <span class="t-main"><span class="t-title">Part of your desktop</span><span class="t-artist">MPRIS · Now Playing · SMTC</span></span>
        <span class="t-badges"><span class="badge">Soon</span></span>
        <span class="t-wave" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span class="t-dur mono">03:47</span>
      </summary>
      <div class="t-notes"><p>Media keys and system controls on every OS: MPRIS on Linux, Now Playing on macOS, SMTC on Windows. Your keyboard's play key just works.</p></div>
    </details></li>

    <li class="reveal" style="--d:5"><details class="track">
      <summary>
        <span class="t-index"><span class="num">06</span><span class="eq"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></span></span>
        <span class="t-art" style="--a:#FF8A52;--b:#141210;--r:200deg"></span>
        <span class="t-main"><span class="t-title">Keyboard first</span><span class="t-artist">Ctrl K · Space · paste a link</span></span>
        <span class="t-badges"><span class="badge">Keys</span></span>
        <span class="t-wave" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span class="t-dur mono">01:31</span>
      </summary>
      <div class="t-notes"><p><kbd>Ctrl</kbd><kbd>K</kbd> to search, <kbd>Space</kbd> to play, and paste any SoundCloud link anywhere in the window to play it right away.</p></div>
    </details></li>

    <li class="reveal" style="--d:6"><details class="track">
      <summary>
        <span class="t-index"><span class="num">07</span><span class="eq"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></span></span>
        <span class="t-art" style="--a:#FF9A1F;--b:#7A2A00;--r:45deg"></span>
        <span class="t-main"><span class="t-title">Your library</span><span class="t-artist">likes · playlists · feed · following</span></span>
        <span class="t-badges"><span class="badge">Sign in</span></span>
        <span class="t-wave" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span class="t-dur mono">05:01</span>
      </summary>
      <div class="t-notes"><p>Sign in through SoundCloud's own web sign-in, and your likes, playlists, feed and followings are there. The token lives in your OS keychain, never in plain text.</p></div>
    </details></li>

    <li class="reveal" style="--d:7"><details class="track">
      <summary>
        <span class="t-index"><span class="num">08</span><span class="eq"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></span></span>
        <span class="t-art" style="--a:#E84D00;--b:#FFF1E8;--r:120deg"></span>
        <span class="t-main"><span class="t-title">Remembers where you were</span><span class="t-artist">queue · position · volume</span></span>
        <span class="t-badges"><span class="badge">Restore</span></span>
        <span class="t-wave" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span class="t-dur mono">04:44</span>
      </summary>
      <div class="t-notes"><p>Close it mid-song. Open it tomorrow. The queue, the position and the volume come back, paused, right where you left them.</p></div>
    </details></li>
  </ol>
</section>

<script>
  import "../scripts/tracklist.js";
</script>
